# UI Design Constitution

`docs/UI_DESIGN_CONSTITUTION.md` is the enshrined visual design document for FRAME. It is the authority for which token and which shared class a piece of content uses.

Before creating or restyling a page, component, or style:

1. Read `docs/UI_DESIGN_CONSTITUTION.md`.
2. Use the existing role. Do not invent a page-specific size, color, or weight.
3. If the visual language itself must change, update the shared class or the theme token, and update the constitution in the same change.

Roles already settled:

- Work synopsis: `.synopsis`
- Page introduction: `.lede`
- One-line review impression: `.impression-line`
- Review comment: `.prose` at `--text-meta` (muted in lists and excerpts, primary on the evaluation page)
- Fact values: `--text-meta`, primary
- Buttons: `.btn` plus one variant (`btn-primary`, `btn-secondary`, `btn-ghost`)

Tokens live in `src/design-system/themes/`. Shared classes live in `src/design-system/components.css`. The constitution decides when each is used. Mood and light/dark change token values only.
